{
  "contract": "settings-search.v1",
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "notes": "The settings the web's Settings search finds (botiverse/slock packages/shared/src/settingsSearch.v1.json; rules: raft-design design/products/raft-chat/settings.md#searching-settings). The App keeps its own index (artin, #proj-raft-ui:#204), using the same id for the same setting where it can, so /settings/<page>#<id> opens the web's page at that setting from either. Names, descriptions, sections and pages are the web's own strings, looked up by id; this file holds where a setting is, which of the web and the desktop app have it, and the other words people use for it. `page` is the web settings slug. `experimental`: not shown in results. `aliases`: other words per display locale; a locale without its own list uses en, and en is always searched too. Where a setting's row has no description (HelperText step 1 cut it), its aliases keep that description's key terms, in each display locale, so the old words still find it.",
